    "title": "Intel calls off planned sale of Folsom campus - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brett Stover ,\n8 hours ago\n(FOX40.COM) — Nearly two years after announcing plans to sell and lease back its Folsom campus, the technology company confirmed Wednesday it has called off the sale.\n\"After careful consideration, Intel has decided not to move forward with the sale and partial leaseback of our Folsom site,\" an Intel spokesperson told FOX40 in an email. \"We remain committed to the Folsom campus and have determined that retaining ownership best supports our long-term objectives.\"\nVIDEO: Nearly 300 Intel employees to be laid off from Folsom campus (October 2024)\nAfter cutting hundreds of jobs at the site, Intel announced in November 2024 it would sell the 161.78-acre campus as part of a company-wide mission to reduce unused space and \"foster greater in-person collaboration.\"\nIntel did not plan to fully abandon Folsom, however, as it planned to lease back part of the campus, which contains about 1.67 million square feet of office space.\nNow, the company is reversing course. A spokesperson said the reversal, first reported by the Sacramento Business Journal, is the result of a strategic reassessment and is \"not a reflection of the quality or competitiveness of the proposals received.\"\nOperations at the site remain unchanged, an Intel spokesperson said.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX40 News.\n3",
    "summary": "(FOX40.COM) — Nearly two years after announcing plans to sell and lease back its Folsom campus, the technology company confirmed Wednesday it has called off the sale. \"We remain committed to the Folsom campus and have determined that retaining ownership best supports our long-term objectives.\" VIDEO: Nearly 300 Intel employees to be laid off from Folsom campus (October 2024) After cutting hundreds of jobs at the site, Intel announced in November 2024 it would sell the 161.78-acre campus as part of a company-wide mission to reduce unused space and \"foster greater in-person collaboration.\"",
